    {
      "id": "zwzpbaBUZyO_RJWDtlscs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 397.35416666666697,
      "y": 3302.8906249999995,
      "width": 995.679931640625,
      "height": 340,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 233100528,
      "version": 1659,
      "versionNonce": 99799056,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1778163938697,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Auto Scaling takes time to spin up and it can take 2 - 3 mins for new servers to spin up. Requests can go from 0 - 1M\nin the fraction of a second. Auto scaling is useless, the system would die even before it has time to auto scale.\nWe must use pre-warming.\nWe must over provision resources - LB, API Gateway, worker nodes must be manually over provisioned hours before the \nsale based on expected marketing research.\nWe will also have multiple tier rate limiting. We will have edge L7 web application firewall deployed at the network edge that\ninspects application layer HTTP traffic to filter out, malicious requests and bots.\nIn flash sale systems, it is critical for protection by implementing a rate limiting, DDos protection, bot detection to prevent \nabuse while ensuring legitimate users can access the website during sale.\n\nWe can also have API token bucket. Restricts legitimate users to 1 checkout request per second.\nPressing buy button too many times can be handled with 429, Too many requests directly from the edge and thereby saving \nnetwork bandwidth.\n\nNext, we also have the Apache Kafka as the shock absorber thereby decoupling the high ingestion rate vs the slow database\nprocessing. So if API layers gets 50,000 reservations in 2 sec, Kafka stores them in disk, and Postgres layer can process the \nrequests at a safe rate.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Auto Scaling takes time to spin up and it can take 2 - 3 mins for new servers to spin up. Requests can go from 0 - 1M\nin the fraction of a second. Auto scaling is useless, the system would die even before it has time to auto scale.\nWe must use pre-warming.\nWe must over provision resources - LB, API Gateway, worker nodes must be manually over provisioned hours before the \nsale based on expected marketing research.\nWe will also have multiple tier rate limiting. We will have edge L7 web application firewall deployed at the network edge that\ninspects application layer HTTP traffic to filter out, malicious requests and bots.\nIn flash sale systems, it is critical for protection by implementing a rate limiting, DDos protection, bot detection to prevent \nabuse while ensuring legitimate users can access the website during sale.\n\nWe can also have API token bucket. Restricts legitimate users to 1 checkout request per second.\nPressing buy button too many times can be handled with 429, Too many requests directly from the edge and thereby saving \nnetwork bandwidth.\n\nNext, we also have the Apache Kafka as the shock absorber thereby decoupling the high ingestion rate vs the slow database\nprocessing. So if API layers gets 50,000 reservations in 2 sec, Kafka stores them in disk, and Postgres layer can process the \nrequests at a safe rate.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
